  "info": {
    "contact": {
      "email": "support@vaquill.ai",
      "name": "Vaquill API Support",
      "url": "https://www.vaquill.ai"
    },
    "description": "Public API for Indian primary law: Central and State Acts, the instruments of the principal regulators, and their individual sections.\n\n**Authentication**: Pass your API key via the `Authorization: Bearer vq_key_...` header. The same key works against the US API; the two share one credit balance.\n\n**Credits**: Each call costs API credits. See `GET /api/v1/api-credits/pricing` for the full pricing matrix.\n\n## Coverage\n\n| Layer | Volume |\n|---|---|\n| Enactments (Central, State and UT) | 22,265 |\n| Individually addressable provisions | 1,098,577 |\n| Regulator instruments | roughly half the corpus |\n\nRegulators covered include SEBI, RBI, MCA, IRDAI, TRAI, DGFT, MOEFCC and CPCB. Every section carries a `sourceUrl` pointing at the publisher's own document.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis document describes the **India** surface only. US statutes are a separate document at `/external/openapi.json`, so an MCP client configured here sees Indian tools and nothing else.",
    "license": {
      "name": "Proprietary",
      "url": "https://www.vaquill.ai/terms"
    },
    "termsOfService": "https://www.vaquill.ai/terms",
    "title": "Vaquill India API",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/in/acts/corresponding-provisions/{act_code}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Section-by-section mapping from a repealed Indian criminal code to the 2023\ncode that replaced it, in force from 1 July 2025.\n\nPass either side of the pair: `ipc` and `bns` both return the IPC to BNS\nmapping, `crpc` and `bnss` both return CrPC to BNSS.\n\n**Coverage**: `ipc`/`bns` and `crpc`/`bnss`. `iea`/`bsa` are accepted but\nreturn 404 until the Evidence Act mapping lands, rather than an empty list\nthat would read as \"nothing changed\".\n\n**Authentication**: API key via `Authorization: Bearer vq_key_...`\n\n**Cost**: 1 credit",
        "operationId": "get_corresponding_provisions_api_v1_in_acts_corresponding_provisions__act_code__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "Act code: ipc, crpc, iea, bns, bnss or bsa",
            "in": "path",
            "name": "act_code",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Act code: ipc, crpc, iea, bns, bnss or bsa",
              "pattern": "^(?i:ipc|crpc|iea|bns|bnss|bsa)$",
              "title": "Act Code",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CorrespondingProvisionsResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Map a repealed code to its replacement",
        "tags": [
          "Indian Acts & Legislation"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/in/acts/filters": {
      "get": {
        "description": "List every value accepted by the `category`, `state`, and `department` filters\non `POST /acts/search`, with the number of sections behind each.\n\n**Authentication**: API key via `Authorization: Bearer vq_key_...`\n\n**Cost**: free.\n\nValues are lowercase and hyphenated (`madhya-pradesh`, `law-commission`).\n`POST /acts/search` rejects anything not listed here with HTTP 422, so read\nthis rather than guessing. Counts are read from the corpus and refresh as\ningest runs land, so treat the list as live rather than caching it in your app.",
        "operationId": "list_act_filters_api_v1_in_acts_filters_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ActFiltersResponse"
